're asking you very specifically so  don't try to  assume that we're trying to get a  different answer from you or that it's a  trick question  answer the question and answer it in  full  um allison that would be my piece what  about you  yeah i think the trick question goes to  that often  you know you might be overthinking the  question  uh when we ask what matters most to you  and why we're really asking that and i  think the common blunder i see there is  sometimes people  end up kind of writing an um mini  autobiography of themselves  and that's not actually the question the  question of what matters most to you  and why um and i think we mentioned with  the recommenders you know  sort of the one sentence answers which  again  you don't have complete control over but  i think that's part of  you know managing your your recommender  um and then i guess the the other one is  is the uh you know using an essay  from for another school and trying to  uh i'm gonna squeeze it in and make it  fit this  this this question even though it  doesn't quite fit  yeah so uh yeah yes  yeah absolutely and as i think has been  said in a number of other sessions  authenticity is so important to this  process and if you are  trying to pose as who you think we want  to read about  then i think that is also a application  a common application blunder  our goal in this process is to get to  know you not somebody who you think we  want to  admit so be authentic be true to  yourself  you are you are the person we're  interested in learning about  so um i think definitely  take that time to reflect and to  fill out your application thoughtfully  and reflect on these questions really  thoroughly  i'm so glad you said that jessica  because it's one that's i think hard to  talk about but as one of our colleagues  say  it's like only you can be the best you  that you can be  so you know you really sort of cheat  yourself  if you're trying to sort of package and  everything is so  perfect it'